# Project Design Phase

## Project Title
Implement Client Script and UI Policy – Incident

## Project Objective
The objective of this project is to implement Client Scripts and UI Policies in ServiceNow Incident Management to improve form behavior, validation, and user experience.

## Project Design

### 1. Client Script
A Client Script will be used to control the Incident form dynamically on the client side.

Functions:
- Validate user-entered data.
- Automatically populate required fields.
- Display messages when incorrect data is entered.
- Change field values based on user actions.

### 2. UI Policy
A UI Policy will be used to dynamically control the Incident form fields.

Functions:
- Make fields mandatory when required.
- Make fields visible or hidden based on conditions.
- Make fields read-only when necessary.

### 3. Incident Form
The project will be implemented on the ServiceNow Incident form using appropriate conditions and actions.

## Expected Outcome
The Incident form should respond dynamically to user actions. Client Scripts will handle client-side logic, while UI Policies will control field visibility, mandatory status, and read-only behavior.

## Tools and Technologies
- ServiceNow
- Client Scripts
- UI Policies
- Incident Management
- JavaScript

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates how Client Scripts and UI Policies can be implemented in ServiceNow to create a more efficient, user-friendly, and controlled Incident Management form.
